# What is NOT uploaded to Vercel.
#
# This file replaces .gitignore rather than adding to it: once it exists, the
# CLI stops consulting .gitignore entirely. So everything secret or large is
# repeated here even where .gitignore already covers it. Leaving a rule out of
# this file is how a local .env reaches a public deployment.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

node_modules/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The local library: uploaded PDFs, the SQLite database and every extracted
# figure crop. Tens of megabytes of one person's reading, which has no business
# on a public instance that builds its own library from scratch.
data/

# README media is served by GitHub and never requested from the deployment.
docs/media/

# Everything the deep tier needs. None of it fits in a serverless bundle, and
# runtime.py already reports those capabilities unavailable here with a reason.
requirements-server.txt

# The float PyTorch weights and the download lock directory. Only the quantised
# ONNX export beside them is loaded at runtime: 23 MB against this one's 88 MB,
# and the bundle limit is what decides whether dense retrieval ships at all.
Semantic Models/models--sentence-transformers--all-MiniLM-L6-v2/
Semantic Models/.locks/
Semantic Models/CACHEDIR.TAG

.git/
.github/
.DS_Store
